READING IT: 50% is NOT the reference. Bars are discrete and a bar
spanning both levels is scored adverse, so the statistic is biased
below 50% even on a driftless path. THE RANDOM CONTROL IS THE
REFERENCE — it carries the same bias at the same risk size. Read
only the gap between the two rows, never a row against 50%.
